 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Well, there's no magic formula. It really depends on how much time and effort you're willing to put into it. Well, I would suggest a combination of both. Learning random words will help you with recognition, but following a list will help you with pronunciation and structure. Yes, reading is definitely a great way to build vocabulary. There are plenty of beginner books out there. You could start with something like 1001 words you need to know, or the complete idiot's guide to Spanish. Both of these books are great for beginners. Yeah, there's a lot of resources available. It's just a matter of finding what works best for you. It's also important to practice regularly.",
